    LLM: 'Game: 500 (Sicilian). Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: '500 Sicilian is a variant of the trick-taking game 500 adapted for the 40-card Sicilian/Italian deck (Coins, Cups, Swords, Clubs; 1-7 + Fante/Cavallo/Re). Bidding for tricks + trump suit. Misère available. Adapted scoring and hand structure for 40-card deck. First to 500 points wins. Kitty/widow for bid winner.',
    objective: 'Reach 500 points first by making and fulfilling bids. Bid for number of tricks and trump (or Misère); bid winner takes the kitty, discards, and must make the contract to score; opponents score tricks they take.',
    gameplay: 'Bid for tricks + trump. Winner takes kitty, discards. Follow suit, trump if void. Misère = lose all tricks. Make contract: score bid value. Fail: lose bid value. Non-bidders score tricks won.',
